{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc","id":123023,"title":"Implied teaser about the Deceived in Cursed Necropolis DC?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-01T01:40:11-07:00","id":123023,"title":"Implied teaser about the Deceived in Cursed Necropolis DC?","content":"Hi all, <br /> <br /> So in the opening credits of the Cursed Necropolis DC book it has a little picture and a &quot;coming soon&quot; add. Pretty standard and innocuous for an ongoing game line like Mummy and Demon.<br /> <br /> (Notice that there is no such &quot;coming soon&quot; at the start of Mortal Remains, as the Hunter line was technically &quot;limited&quot; (as in a set number of books) and as such has &quot;ended&quot;) <br /> <br /> I kinda glossed over it, but then I remembered an old post by CAS on these forums. He mentioned that each of the starting chapter full page art pieces in Mummy represented a signature character. <br /> <br /> For example I believe the Maa-Kep signature character is on the front Cover of Guildhalls. <br /> <br /> Likewise, according to CAS the Shaunkshen signature character &quot;The Roller&quot; is depicted as the full page art of the chapter &quot;Faces of Undeath&quot; in the storytellers section of the core book. <br /> <br /> So the full page art for &quot;The Modeler&quot; (Chapter 2 of the Players section of the core book) is used as the Book of the Deceived art piece for Book of the Deceived in the DC &quot;coming soon&quot; credit section. Implying this will be the cover art for Book of the Deceived and that the woman depicted is the Deceived signature character. <br /> <br /> Interestingly, the fiction at preludes that picture is about an Arisen passing through Heathrow Airport and being kinda amazed by the modern world. The woman he sees strikes him because she is blond and blue eyed, characteristics that simply did not exist in the population of the Nameless Empire. <br /> <br /> IF, and its a big IF, this is the signature Deceived character that is interesting and leads to some interesting ideas and possibilities. <br /> <br /> Its possible that the Deceived have a more &quot;flexible&quot; Sahu that allows them to blend in with the local population authenticity even more then the Arisen. Alternatively it could suggest abilities to alter their appearance. Certainly it suggests an ability to appear as completely mortal to the Arisen. Most interestingly, perhaps the Deceived can possess Mortals? Or maybe they are embodied in modern bodies ala Mummy the Resurrection? <br /> <br /> Of course I could just be massively reading too much into this and be half remembering an old post of CAS. Still food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T01:48:42-07:00","id":123026,"title":"","content":"That's not the only Deceived spoiler in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T02:04:41-07:00","id":123028,"title":"","content":"To be fair. I've only read the introduction so far. Mortal Remains and real life are keeping me from the rest for now. Probably take me a few days to get through it. Still, I thought if fun that the first tease might actually be before the introduction even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T04:39:39-07:00","id":123064,"title":"","content":"It might just be a place-holder image","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T04:51:21-07:00","id":123069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc?p=123064#post123064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might just be a place-holder image</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I know, hence my disclaimer at the end of my first post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />- <br /> <br /> <b><i>&quot;Of course I could just be massively reading too much into this and be half remembering an old post of CAS.&quot;</i></b><br /> <br /> Still, if it is a subtle tease/hint thing then I'd say its a VERY subtle one. Or maybe I am just desperate enough try and deduce anything new about Deceived that I'm seeing hints where their are none. Hell, if nothing else getting the possible hint and creating this topic managed to destroy what would have otherwise been a boring 20 minutes...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Oh yeah the other thing -<br /> <br /> Hopefully it will get people talking about more concrete hints/teases/spoilers for Deceived in DC and what they might imply/mean...maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:06:14-07:00","id":123202,"title":"","content":"I took the heathrow airport character to be a Su Menent. The various references to being a &quot;Godly Mystic&quot; gave a very priest-y feel. Also, it shouldn't really require a mummy to have any sort of flexible sahu to pass unnoticed in heathrow: london has extremely significant black, south asian, and middle-eastern populations (I think within the city white europeans are actually the minority, which makes TV London about as inaccurate as TV New York). And even if that weren't true, someone from far away would certainly not be out of place in one of the biggest <i>international airports</i> in the world. <br /> <br /> In short, yeah, I suspect you're way over-assuming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:16:59-07:00","id":123208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc?p=123202#post123202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I took the heathrow airport character to be a Su Menent. The various references to being a &quot;Godly Mystic&quot; gave a very priest-y feel. Also, it shouldn't really require a mummy to have any sort of flexible sahu to pass unnoticed in heathrow: london has extremely significant black, south asian, and middle-eastern populations (I think within the city white europeans are actually the minority, which makes TV London about as inaccurate as TV New York). And even if that weren't true, someone from far away would certainly not be out of place in one of the biggest <i>international airports</i> in the world.<br /> <br /> In short, yeah, I suspect you're way over-assuming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, very, very likely. Still shot in the dark and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T11:41:37-07:00","id":123313,"title":"","content":"References to the Deceived later in the book also suggest some power of disguise. This character from the opening fic might be a pawn of the Deceived but seems somewhat more likely to be one of them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Perhaps you should have been an artist,&quot; the man's voice said.<br /> <br /> Seb-Hetchet looked up, the fog boiling off in bright and sudden sunlight. His eyes focused, not without effort, past the golden glare that surrounded the stranger sitting across from him - a white man, thin and fiercely bearded, stroking a red-haired mane that partly concealed a high collar above an expensive suit. Dim grey eyes peered from behind spectacles. For the briefest of moments, Seb-Hetchet thought the man's features mismatched, but the sense of asymmetry subsided amidst the glimmer. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T11:49:59-07:00","id":123327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc#post123023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Notice that there is no such &quot;coming soon&quot; at the start of Mortal Remains, as the Hunter line was technically &quot;limited&quot; (as in a set number of books) and as such has &quot;ended&quot;)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Off topic, and I'm not sure if you meant this as literally as I'm reading it, but I'm pretty sure that's no longer true. Especially considering that Dark Eras is coming soon--and Rich has been hinting about something for Geist, the most limited of all the limited run games, that will be announced at GenCon (unless I'm completely misreading his posts). Also, given Matt's comment about the potential for a Hunter Chronicle book in some possible future, I wouldn't say it's ended. It's just that there's nothing on the slate at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T12:29:19-07:00","id":123353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc?p=123327#post123327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Off topic, and I'm not sure if you meant this as literally as I'm reading it, but I'm pretty sure that's no longer true. Especially considering that Dark Eras is coming soon--and Rich has been hinting about something for Geist, the most limited of all the limited run games, that will be announced at GenCon (unless I'm completely misreading his posts). Also, given Matt's comment about the potential for a Hunter Chronicle book in some possible future, I wouldn't say it's ended. It's just that there's nothing on the slate at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough.<br /> <br /> Geist never got a proper run due to the business issues White Wolf experienced shortly after its release. Changeling and Hunter have had several additional releases since their lines &quot;ended&quot;. As you say, it likely that Hunter, at current (or as far as the schedule the devs can show the public is concerned) does not have another project slated at this time.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Mummy and Demon have yet to finish even their original book run, hence the more &quot;coming soon&quot; thing inherent in those lines. <br /> <br /> Rich seemed to be hinting at a lot of things in the last Monday Meeting Notes. Changeling the Dreaming and Changeling the Lost news, Geist news and the new game line. GenCon is going to blow the doors of next year I think.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm hoping Onyx Path manage to fit a Promethean, Changeling and Geist Chronicle book into 2015. That would fit with &quot;news&quot; for Changeling and Geist. The Promethean one is perhaps just wishful thinking on my part.<br /> <br /> Anyway...back on topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T14:35:59-07:00","id":123419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc?p=123353#post123353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rich seemed to be hinting at a lot of things in the last Monday Meeting Notes. Changeling the Dreaming and Changeling the Lost news, Geist news and the new game line. GenCon is going to blow the doors of next year I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, Onyx Path at GenCon is gonna blow some minds. They've been planning the 2015 schedule for a long time, as I understand it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc?p=123353#post123353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I'm hoping Onyx Path manage to fit a Promethean, Changeling and Geist Chronicle book into 2015. That would fit with &quot;news&quot; for Changeling and Geist. The Promethean one is perhaps just wishful thinking on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>My Big Theory (and I'm fine if I end up being wrong; I have nothing but gut feelings and circumstantial evidence) is that Promethean, Changeling and Geist are gonna get their Chronicle books. At the BARE minimum (if there are conversions coming) we'll see Mortal Remains-like supplements with basic conversions, but I have a feeling it's gonna be bigger--I have a dim fantasy that a Stretch Goal or some such for Dark Eras is going to include a quick guide to GMC rule patch ups.<br /> <br /> I hear that Black Hat Matt is dying to do a Promethean Chronicle, so cross your fingers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/123023-implied-teaser-about-the-deceived-in-cursed-necropolis-dc?p=123353#post123353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway...back on topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so bad at picking up clues for this sort of thing, but it does seem like the opening fiction is hinting at something Deceived related.<br /> <br /> Here's the one I noticed from the opening fiction: Set favours the red haired...<br /> <br /> And at the end, Seb-Hetchet is specifically &quot;deceived.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 05-01-2014, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T12:13:16-07:00","id":125289,"title":"","content":"Well, having actually finished reading the book now I can safely say their are some pretty epic teases for Deceived which are much more then just implied...<br /> <br /> Bloody hell the Lost Guild are looking to be more powerful, knowledgeable and epic then even I suspected from Guildhalls teasers. So can't wait for Book of the Deceived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img